meta {
  name: Get Product Subpaths
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06/attributes
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data.brand: eq Plytix
}

docs {
  `GET /api/v3/products/{identifier}/{path}` — fetch a single expanded subresource
  of a product. The primary request here runs `/attributes`; see the examples below
  for `/categories`, `/assets`, `/relationships`, and `/static_lists`. Confirmed
  live 2026-09-07/08 against "David's Dev Account"; re-verified (and a critical
  regression found) 2026-09-23.

  ## ⚠️ CRITICAL, confirmed 2026-09-23 — `/categories`, `/assets`, `/static_lists` subpaths are broken
  All three now reliably return `{"data": [], "errors": []}` — **always empty** —
  regardless of real, confirmed linkage. Reproduced on multiple products, including
  a fresh scratch product created and linked in the same test run (categories and
  a thumbnail asset both set on `POST`, confirmed present via `_fields` immediately
  after), and against the long-lived reference fixture `BAG-10157`, which still
  genuinely has 2 categories and 11 assets (confirmed via the workaround below) —
  its subpath responses are just as broken as the fresh product's.

  **Confirmed correct workaround**: request the same data via `_fields` on the
  search/list endpoint instead of the dedicated subpath —
  `GET /products?_fields=categories&_fields=assets&_fields=static_lists&sku=...`
  (or filtered any other way) returns the real, fully expanded data every time.
  See `List Products.bru`'s "Full Parameters (Relationship Fields Expanded)"
  example for a captured response.

  **Why this matters for docs**: the dedicated `/{identifier}/{path}` subpath
  route — previously documented as the way to fetch expanded relationship data —
  can no longer be recommended for `categories`, `assets`, or `static_lists`.
  This caused a real, documented false-positive earlier in this project: an
  earlier session concluded `static_list_ids` silently no-ops on `PATCH` because
  it checked via `GET /products/{id}/static_lists` (empty) instead of `_fields`
  (which correctly shows the link) — see `Update Product (PATCH).bru`'s
  corrected "200 - Full Parameters" example. Report this to Plytix as a
  regression; `/relationships` and `/attributes` (both confirmed still working
  below) show the subpath *mechanism* itself isn't gone, just these three
  specific relations.

  ## Confirmed valid subpaths on products
  | Path | Returns | Status as of 2026-09-23 |
  |---|---|---|
  | `/attributes` | Full attributes map as `data` | ✅ Working |
  | `/attributes/<name>` | Single attribute value as `data` | ✅ Working — e.g. `data: "Plytix"` |
  | `/categories` | Array of expanded `ProductCategoryGetOutputDto` | ❌ Broken — always empty (Bug). Use `_fields=categories` on search instead. |
  | `/assets` | Array of expanded `AssetOutputDto` | ❌ Broken — always empty (Bug). Use `_fields=assets` on search instead. |
  | `/relationships` | Flat array of `{relationship_id, relationship_label, product_id}` | ✅ Working — different (flatter) shape than the `product_relationships` object in a full GET |
  | `/static_lists` | Array of Static product lists this product belongs to | ❌ Broken — always empty (Bug). Use `_fields=static_lists` on search instead. Smart list membership still has no product-side trace at all (a separate, non-bug limitation) — see Static Lists example. |

  ## Subpath-discovery 400 trick (applies to all v3 resources)
  Hitting `GET /{resource}/{id}/{bogus_path}` with an unrecognised `{path}` returns
  `400 {"errors":[{"name":"ValueError","description":"Field '<path>' not found.
  Available fields: [...]"}]}` listing the resource's raw internal model fields.
  For products: `['id','account_id','sku','label','gtin','status','attributes',
  'thumbnail_id','parent_id','num_variations','product_level','product_family_id',
  'product_family_model_id','overwritten_attributes','mark_as_deleted',
  'product_relationships','created','modified','last_context',
  'modified_user_audit','created_user_audit']`.
  Caveat: this raw list does NOT include computed/joined relations (`categories`,
  `assets`, `relationships`) that are still valid subpaths (all confirmed 200).
  Use this trick early in each new resource phase before guessing subpath names.

  ## Assets subpath spot-check findings
  `GET /assets/{id}/{path}` tested directly against asset id `6a38f5e1c3d65a5f868b18a5`:
  - `/categories` → 200, `[]` (asset not in any category).
  - `/attributes`, `/relationships`, `/products` → all **400** (`ValueError`) —
    assets have no attributes/relationships concept and there is no
    reverse `assets/{id}/products` lookup.

  ## Static lists: Smart list membership has no product-side trace
  `GET /products/{id}/static_lists` reflects only Static list membership. The
  Smart list (`6aa0322d2b6fd055ffb7cabb`) that matches this product via its `sku`
  filter does NOT appear anywhere on the product. The only way to discover Smart
  list membership is to re-execute the list's own `query` against `GET /products`
  — there is no reverse-lookup from the product side for dynamic/Smart lists.

  ## Relationships: two distinct shapes
  The `/relationships` subpath returns a flat `[{relationship_id, relationship_label,
  product_id}]` array — a different (flatter) summary than the nested
  `product_relationships: {<label>: [{quantity, last_modified}]}` object embedded
  in a full `GET /products/{id}`. Neither matches `openapi_pimv3.json`'s
  `relationships` field name. See `Get Product by ID.bru` for context.
}

example {
  name: 200 - Attributes Subpath (Full Map)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-07. The attributes map is returned directly as data (same object embedded under data.attributes on a full GET /products/{id}). Also confirmed: GET /products/{id}/attributes/<name> returns just the single value (e.g. data: "Plytix").

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06/attributes
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "brand": "Plytix",
            "color": "Black",
            "amazon_ready": 85.71,
            "basic_information_completeness": 100.0,
            "google_shopping_completeness": 92.86,
            "website_ready": 100.0
          },
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: 200 - Categories Subpath (Broken, Always Empty) (Bug)
  description: CONFIRMED HAZARD, live 2026-09-23. BAG-10157 genuinely has 2 categories (confirmed via GET /products?_fields=categories&sku=BAG-10157 — see List Products.bru) but this dedicated subpath returns an empty array regardless. Superseded 2026-09-07 example claimed 2 expanded category objects — that was accurate at the time but no longer reflects live behavior. Do not use this subpath for categories; use _fields=categories on the search endpoint instead.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06/categories
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [],
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

