example {
  name: 200 - Relationships Subpath (Flat Summary)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-07, re-verified live 2026-09-23 -- still working (unlike /categories, /assets, /static_lists above). Returns a flat array of {relationship_id, relationship_label, product_id}, different from the nested product_relationships object embedded in GET /products/{id}. relationship_label=related_products confirmed via assertion. Note: relationship_id and product_id both drifted from the original 2026-09-07 capture (was relationship_id ...186b / product_id ...1a07) to the current values below, including product_id now matching BAG-10157's own id (self-referential) -- captured verbatim as the current live ground truth, not corrected or interpreted.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06/relationships
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [
            {
              "relationship_id": "6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b186c",
              "relationship_label": "related_products",
              "product_id": "6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06"
            }
          ],
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: 200 - static_lists Subpath (Broken, Always Empty) (Bug)
  description: CONFIRMED HAZARD, live 2026-09-23. WC-TEST-FULL-001 genuinely IS a member of "WC Test Static List" (confirmed via GET /products?_fields=static_lists&sku=WC-TEST-FULL-001 — see List Products.bru) but this dedicated subpath returns an empty array regardless. Superseded 2026-09-08 example claimed 1 Static list membership — that was accurate at the time but no longer reflects live behavior. This is the same bug that earlier caused a false-positive report that PATCH's static_list_ids silently no-ops (see Update Product (PATCH).bru's corrected full-parameters example). Do not use this subpath for static list membership; use _fields=static_lists on the search endpoint instead. Smart list membership still has no product-side trace at all regardless (a separate, pre-existing, non-bug limitation).

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6aa022262b6fd055ffb7caa4/static_lists
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [],
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
